 For a folder plan "the plan" means every file in the change folder, and the digest is the one `--freeze-plan` printed. The plan must already be in its final state, including its own merge-gate checkbox (final verification wave F2) marked `[x]`, at the moment reviewers are dispatched and this digest is taken - no plan edit may follow. `plan_sha256` binds whatever bytes existed at hash time, so hashing before that mark would seal an unfrozen plan and let the gate's own required output invalidate its own binding.
 
